WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.525
Step three runs two days
against the fictional tenant.

2
00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:08.154
First, one variable holds the run's
settings: the cloud, the tenant I D,

3
00:00:08.154 --> 00:00:12.615
the output folder, the audit
fixture, the emergency access files,

4
00:00:12.615 --> 00:00:17.412
the exceptions, the Azure scopes,
and the control-plane subscription.

5
00:00:17.412 --> 00:00:22.075
Then run day one, as of six in the
morning on the twenty-ninth of October.

6
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:26.798
The inventory, the emergency check
and the PIM audit read all report OK,

7
00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:30.300
and the audit window is the
twenty-four hours before.

8
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.525
Then day two, against the second
day's tenant, as of the thirtieth.

9
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:38.937
Notice the second window starts
exactly where the first ended: no gap.

10
00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:43.500
Each run's folder has a run file that
lists each task's manifest hash.

11
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.934
On your machine, the Written to line
may print the folder's full path;

12
00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.740
the path's verification log records that.
